# GLM-5.3-Flash with its experts cut to 144 per layer (REAP), calibrated on coding
# sessions, at 4 bits: 98 GB, where glm-5.3-flash is the whole model at 2 bits. The card
# reports 48 of 48 agentic tasks at a 384k window and perplexity 22.7% above the whole
# model at 8 bits. Published 2026-10-14, so hardly anyone has tried it yet. MIT.
TITLE="GLM-5.3-Flash, REAP 144 Coder"
DETAIL="pruned to 144 experts, 18B active, 4-bit GGUF, 98 GB"
HF_REPO=lapadatbogdan/GLM-5.3-Flash-REAP144-Coder-GGUF
HF_INCLUDE="*Q4_K_M*"
GGUF_MATCH="Q4_K_M"
ALIAS=glm-5.3-flash-reap-coder
CTX=fit
CTX_MIN=262144
FIT_MARGIN_MB=8192
KV_TYPE=f16
MIN_FREE_GB=100
EXTRA_ARGS="--load-mode dio --cache-ram 0 --timeout 14400 --reasoning on --reasoning-format auto"
